msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2016/real-process-memory-in-python.rst:100
msgid "Memory type percent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2016/real-process-memory-in-python.rst:102
msgid ""
"After reorganizing the process memory APIs (:pr:`744`), I added a new "
"``memtype`` parameter to :meth:`Process.memory_percent`. You can now compare "
"a specific memory type (not only :term:`RSS`) against the total physical "
"memory. E.g."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2016/real-process-memory-in-python.rst:107
msgid ""
">>> psutil.Process().memory_percent(memtype='pss')\n"
"0.06877466326787016"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2016/real-process-memory-in-python.rst:113
msgid "Process environ"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2016/real-process-memory-in-python.rst:115
msgid ""
"The second biggest improvement in psutil 4.0.0 is the ability to read a "
"process's environment variables. This opens up interesting possibilities for "
"process recognition and monitoring. For instance, you can start a process "
"with a custom environment variable, then iterate over all processes to find "
"the one of interest:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2016/real-process-memory-in-python.rst:121
msgid ""
"import psutil\n"
"for p in psutil.process_iter():\n"
"    try:\n"
"        env = p.environ()\n"
"    except psutil.Error:\n"
"        pass\n"
"    else:\n"
"        if 'MYAPP' in env:\n"
"            ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2016/real-process-memory-in-python.rst:133
msgid ""
"Process environ was a long-standing issue (:gh:`52`, from 2009) that I gave "
"up on because the Windows implementation only worked for the current "
"process. `Frank Benkstein <https://github.com/fbenkstein>`_ solved that (:pr:"
"`747`), and it now works on Linux, Windows and macOS for all processes (you "
"may still hit :exc:`AccessDenied` for processes owned by another user):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2016/real-process-memory-in-python.rst:139
msgid ""
">>> import psutil\n"
">>> from pprint import pprint as pp\n"
">>> pp(psutil.Process().environ())\n"
"{...\n"
" 'CLUTTER_IM_MODULE': 'xim',\n"
" 'COLORTERM': 'gnome-terminal',\n"
" 'COMPIZ_BIN_PATH': '/usr/bin/',\n"
" 'HOME': '/home/giampaolo',\n"
" 'PWD': '/home/giampaolo/svn/psutil',\n"
"  }\n"
">>>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2016/real-process-memory-in-python.rst:153
msgid ""
"Note that the resulting dict usually doesn't reflect changes made after the "
"process started (e.g. ``os.environ['MYAPP'] = '1'``). Again, for anyone "
"porting this to other languages, here are the interesting parts:"
msgstr ""

