#: ../../../blog/2016/real-process-memory-in-python.rst:188
msgid "Porting code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2016/real-process-memory-in-python.rst:190
msgid ""
"Since 4.0.0 is a major version, I took the chance to (lightly) change / "
"break some APIs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2016/real-process-memory-in-python.rst:193
msgid ""
":meth:`Process.memory_info` no longer returns just an (:field:`rss`, :field:"
"`vms`) namedtuple. It returns a variable-length namedtuple that varies by "
"platform (:field:`rss` and :field:`vms` are always present, even on "
"Windows). Essentially the same result as the old :meth:`Process."
"memory_info_ex`. This shouldn't break your code unless you were doing ``rss, "
"vms = p.memory_info()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2016/real-process-memory-in-python.rst:199
msgid ""
":meth:`Process.memory_info_ex` is deprecated. It still works as an alias "
"for :meth:`Process.memory_info`, issuing a :exc:`DeprecationWarning`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2016/real-process-memory-in-python.rst:201
msgid ""
":func:`psutil.disk_io_counters` on NetBSD and OpenBSD no longer returns :"
"field:`write_count` and :field:`read_count` because the kernel doesn't "
"provide them (we were returning the busy time instead). Should be a small "
"issue given NetBSD and OpenBSD support is very recent."
msgstr ""

